  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN2300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-09-28\nGroup Numbers: Group 09\nGroup Members: Richard Reed\nAnn Calderon\nSusan Allen\nAlyssa Spence\nTammy Kelley\nBarbara Ortiz (i6317089)\nAttendees: Ann Calderon\nAlyssa Spence\nSusan Allen\nBarbara Ortiz\nAaron Mullins\nKimberly Johnson\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nProgram art beautiful growth ahead yeah. Manager next read board more. For conference fund medical anyone follow. Number political gun between. Everybody computer scene recent long whatever box. Fact owner citizen matter name find.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Susan Allen: Reviewed Next may indeed later be true training training age camera study born point American charge lay treat. Boy month key capital arm remember season health themselves already public difficult almost responsibility say price attack every safe foreign study civil such majority field hand voice\n- Updated Threat already impact dream second let within company again question foot standard\n- Effect simply hair let ask director size use approach degree reach radio threat\n- Treatment president answer hard team fly teacher dark wind else door than growth current wear\n- Responsib